      "text": "Moriah was carved out of Elizabethtown in 1808, giving the town its own name and borders.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moriah%2C_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Between 1824 and 1971, iron ore mined in the Adirondacks powered industry that shipped goods from Port Henry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27,
        28,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moriah%2C_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Iron Center Museum in Port Henry preserves that industrial heritage with artifacts and stories from the region’s iron era.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moriah%2C_New_York",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Town Historical Society displays railroad and mining history in a restored carriage house, echoing Moriah’s industrial past.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
